.TH SHAIRPORT-SYNC 1
.SH NAME
shairport-sync \- AirPlay 2 receiver for Linux with PulseAudio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shairport-sync
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives realtime and buffered AirPlay 2 audio. PulseAudio, Avahi, OpenSSL,
FFmpeg and compatible NQPTP are required. Missing or incompatible NQPTP causes
startup to fail before listening or advertising. No AirPlay 1 fallback is provided.
PipeWire can be used through its PulseAudio-compatible server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " --version"
Show version and build features.
.TP
.BR \-c " FILE"
Read configuration from FILE.
.TP
.BR \-a " NAME"
Set the advertised receiver name.
.TP
.BR \-p " PORT"
Set RTSP port (default 7000).
.TP
.BR \-v
Increase diagnostic verbosity. May be repeated.
.SH CONFIGURATION
See shairport-sync.conf.sample for PulseAudio server and sink, volume,
channel mapping, network interface, UDP ports and synchronisation settings.
Removed backend, service selection, DSP and metadata-export settings are errors.
.SH SERVICE
Run as a systemd user service belonging to the PulseAudio session owner.
NQPTP and Avahi run separately. No system account or alternate init installer
is provided.
.SH LIMITATIONS
AirPlay 1, alternate backends, DBus, MPRIS, MQTT, DSP and metadata export are
removed. Protocol metadata, encrypted pairing and Home endpoints are retained.
